# Host-installed dependencies must never enter an image: postinstall/compile
# always run inside the container so linked native modules and generated
# artifacts match its OS/arch, not whatever the host happened to build.
**/node_modules

# Compiled output is regenerated by each package's own compile script
# (`clean && build`, which removes it first), so a host checkout's possibly
# stale copy only adds build-context weight without being used.
packages/*/build
packages/*/ts_build

.git
.idea

# `**/` is required for these to match at any depth: unlike .gitignore,
# Docker only anchors a bare pattern to the build context root (confirmed
# empirically -- a bare `artifacts` here silently let
# packages/crypto-rpc/blockchain/EVM/artifacts and cache, Hardhat's own
# regenerated compile output, leak into images built from root context).
**/artifacts
**/cache
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
.DS_Store

# A developer's accumulated runtime logs/pids (wallet-service's own
# start-docker.sh writes these; see its own .gitignore) are host state, not
# source -- found leaking hundreds of MB into a real `COPY . .` build here,
# the same host-state-isolation problem as node_modules above.
**/logs
**/pids
*.log
